--- MESSAGE ---
A valueType is a JSON node, on the same terms as a value

The TypeElement family, Factory, Variable and Case declare `valueType Json`: a string is the type's
authored text, which is everything the corpus holds today, and an object will be a type-form tree —
Atomic, Objective, Parametric, Morphic with Haskell's right-associative arrow — once the drake parser
trees the four forms. Decoded absent-as-Null and elided null-or-empty exactly as `value` is.

The corpus stays strings, so no definition and no generated line moved except the family's own and
DracoAspect's emptiness test. Every consumer reads the type through `TypeForm.text` (`.valueType.text`),
a new shape accessor beside Expression; the engine spells the type for the target once, at the
generate entry, in targetTypes. Family JSON regenerated from the drake and family Scala from the JSON
with the compiled tools.

Next: the parser and emitter learn the four forms and the corpus re-canonicalizes from the drake;
then typeParameters, which lives in TypeName's identity.

